Market Terminal — NOTICE
========================

Attribution
-----------

This project began as a copy of "BBterminal" by Vaughan Fawcett
(https://github.com/vaughanf1/BB-Terminal), taken from upstream commit 74f9176.
The terminal shell, the original function catalogue, the signal classifiers and
the OpenBB integration originate from that work; this repository extends it
(portfolio simulation, execution algorithms, performance/risk analytics,
screener, point-in-time simulation clock, tests, synthetic demo mode, and more).

At the time it was copied, the upstream repository carried no LICENSE file.
Under default copyright, all rights in the upstream code remain with its author.
Nothing in this repository purports to license the upstream author's work.

Independence
------------

Market Terminal is an independent, educational, terminal-style project. It is
not affiliated with, endorsed by, sponsored by, or connected to any financial
data vendor, exchange, broker, or terminal provider. Function codes are short
generic mnemonics chosen for keyboard-driven navigation.

Third-party components
----------------------

- OpenBB Platform (AGPL-3.0) — optional, live mode only. Installed by the user
  as a separate process and reached over its local HTTP API; not bundled or
  modified by this project.
- Live-mode data providers reached through OpenBB (e.g. Yahoo Finance, Finviz,
  Federal Reserve, SEC) are subject to their own terms of service. Personal,
  non-commercial use only. No third-party data is included in this repository.
- JetBrains Mono font via @fontsource/jetbrains-mono (SIL Open Font License 1.1).
- npm dependencies are listed in app/package.json under their own licenses.

Synthetic data
--------------

The default demo mode generates all prices, fundamentals, headlines and option
chains in the browser from a seeded random process (app/src/lib/synthetic.ts).
No real market data is shown in synthetic mode.
